    "filename": "img-4313-1.jpg",
    "localUrl": "/images/gallery/grants/2023/img-4313-1.jpg",
    "altText": "",
    "caption": "Photo of chapter #42 presenting a grant check to the President of Bishop Feehan High School.In the photo are our Chaplain Rev David Costa, Mr. Sullivan and #42 officers Paul and Sheila Pinsonnault.The check was presented at a 100th anniversary Mass for St Mary/Sacred Heart Elementary School. Our chapter has been a strong supporter of the school since it opened in 1923 and continue today. We made it a point to take the picture in front of the St Jean Baptiste statue. Our chapter members in 1904 petitioned Bishop Stang to build a French speaking parish. That was accomplished and the statue has been in the church since the building was finished.",
    "year": "2023"
  },
  {
    "category": "grants",
    "filename": "380967280-270505032536188-128825652816386638-n-1.jpg",
    "localUrl": "/images/gallery/grants/2023/380967280-270505032536188-128825652816386638-n-1.jpg",
    "altText": "",
    "caption": "On September 19th, our chapter delivered the $500.00 check from Saint Jean Baptiste Educational Foundation to East Catholic High School in Manchester Ct.Mr. Sean P. Brennan, President, was very pleased to get this much-needed funds to help existing and future families with the goal of signing up for the best education.He was thrilled to share with us that since the start of the 2021-2022 school year, the freshman class enrollment is up 45%! He stated that this is a testament to their commitment to excellence in academics, athletics, and fine arts.",
    "year": "2023"
  },
